ame>Orth</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Epidermodysplasia verruciformis: a model for understanding the oncogenicity of human papillomaviruses</article-title><source>Ciba Found Symp</source><year>1986</year><volume>120</volume><fpage>157</fpage><lpage>174</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Ciba Found Symp||120|157||bib18|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3013521</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pierceall</surname><given-names>WE</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldberg</surname><given-names>LH</given-names></name><name><surname>Tainsky</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Mukhopadhyay</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Ananthaswamy</surname><given-names>HN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ras gene mutation and amplification in human nonmelanoma skin cancers</article-title><source>Mol Carcinog</source><year>1991</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>196</fpage><lpage>202</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Mol Carcinog||4|196||bib19|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2064725</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Proniewska</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Jablonska</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>UV-induced DNA repair synthesis in patients with epidermodysplasia verruciformis</article-title><source>Dermatologica</source><year>1980</year><volume>160</volume><fpage>289</fpage><lpage>296</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Dermatologica||160|289||bib20|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6244993</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rasheed</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Nelson-Rees</surname><given-names>WA</given-names></name><name><surname>Toth</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Arnstein</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Gardner</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Characterization of a newly derived human sarcoma cell line (HT-1080)</article-title><source>Cancer</source><year>1974</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>1027</fpage><lpage>1033</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer||33|1027||bib21|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4132053</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Surentheran</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Harwood</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Spink</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Sinclair</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Leigh</surname><given-names>IM</given-names></name><name><surname>Proby</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>McGregor</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Breuer</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Detection and typing of human papillomaviruses in mucosal and cutaneous biopsies from immunosuppressed and immunocompetent patients and patients with epidermodysplasia verruciformis: a unified diagnostic approach</article-title><source>J Clin Pathol</source><year>1998</year><volume>51</volume><fpage>606</fpage><lpage>610</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Clin Pathol||51|606||bib22|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9828820</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Therrien</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Drouin</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Baril</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Drobetsky</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Human cells compromised for p53 function exhibit defective global and transcription-coupled nucleotide excision repair, whereas cells compromised for pRb function are defective only in global repair</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>1999</year><volume>96</volume><fpage>15038</fpage><lpage>15043</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Proc Natl Acad Sci USA||96|15038||bib23|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wigler</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sweet</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Sim</surname><given-names>GK</given-names></name><name><surname>Wold</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Pellicer</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Lacy</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Maniatis</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Silverstein</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Axel</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transformation of mammalian cells with genes from procaryotes and eucaryotes</article-title><source>Cell</source><year>1979</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>777</fpage><lpage>785</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cell||16|777||bib24|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">222468</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>